<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="Privacy Policy for Nail Bloom by READY COM.">
  <title>Nail Bloom — Privacy Policy</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: light;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
      color: #302532;
      background: #faf6f8;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body { margin: 0; }
    main {
      max-width: 850px;
      margin: 40px auto;
      padding: 40px;
      background: white;
      border: 1px solid #eedee7;
      border-radius: 20px;
    }
    header {
      border-bottom: 1px solid #eedee7;
      padding-bottom: 24px;
      margin-bottom: 28px;
    }
    .brand {
      color: #92456d;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: .08em;
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 42px);
      line-height: 1.15;
      margin: 12px 0;
    }
    h2 { font-size: 21px; margin-top: 30px; }
    p, li { line-height: 1.75; font-size: 16px; }
    a { color: #82355f; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    a:focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid #b75789;
      outline-offset: 3px;
    }
    .meta { color: #6f6270; }
    footer {
      border-top: 1px solid #eedee7;
      margin-top: 32px;
      padding-top: 20px;
    }
    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      main { margin: 12px; padding: 24px; border-radius: 12px; }
    }
    @media print {
      body { background: white; }
      main { border: 0; margin: 0; max-width: none; padding: 0; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <header>
    <div class="brand">NAIL BLOOM · READY COM</div>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">
      Effective date and last updated: 13 October 2026<br>
      Android application: <strong>com.nailbloom.nailnail</strong>
    </p>
  </header>

  <p>
    READY COM develops Nail Bloom, an app for nail-art lessons, drawing,
    videos, quizzes, and certificates. This policy explains information
    handled by the app and its advertising services. For questions or
    privacy requests, contact
    <a href="mailto:kolonil97@outlook.com">kolonil97@outlook.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information stored on your device</h2>
  <p>
    Nail Bloom does not require an account. Lesson progress, toolkit
    checklists, quiz answers and results, saved nail designs, and
    certificate details are stored locally in the app’s storage.
    If you enter a learner name for a certificate, that name is stored
    locally and included in the certificate you export. READY COM does
    not operate a server to receive or synchronize these items, and the
    app does not intentionally send them to advertising partners.
  </p>
  <p>
    Lessons and bundled tutorial videos can be used offline. The app
    may copy video assets into its local cache for playback. It does
    not request access to your camera, microphone, contacts, or precise
    device location.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Files you export</h2>
  <p>
    You can export a design or certificate as an image using Android’s
    file picker. You choose where it is saved. If you select a
    cloud-storage provider or share the exported file with another app,
    that service handles the file under its own privacy policy.
    Exported copies may remain outside Nail Bloom after you clear its
    storage or uninstall it.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Advertising and third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    Nail Bloom uses Unity LevelPlay (ironSource) for banner and
    interstitial advertising. Its advertising integration includes
    Google AdMob, Meta Audience Network, and Unity Ads. Which partner
    serves an ad depends on availability and the advertising
    configuration.
  </p>
  <p>
    Advertising services may process advertising or other app/device
    identifiers, IP address and approximate location inferred from it,
    device and operating-system details, app version, network
    information, ad impressions and clicks, and diagnostic or
    performance data. SDKs may store information on the device.
    These services use information to deliver ads, personalize ads
    where permitted, measure advertising performance, diagnose
    problems, and prevent fraud or abuse. Advertising and mediation
    providers receive and process information through their SDKs;
    their own policies describe further processing, sharing,
    and retention.
  </p>
  <p>Provider information and privacy choices:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Google:
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
      and
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">
        Advertising information
      </a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Unity, including LevelPlay/ironSource and Unity Ads:
      <a href="https://unity.com/legal/game-player-and-app-user-privacy-policy">
        Game Player and App User Privacy Policy
      </a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Meta Audience Network:
      <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/">
        Meta Privacy Policy
      </a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Consent and advertising choices</h2>
  <p>
    The app uses Google’s User Messaging Platform to request advertising
    consent when required and when a message is configured for your
    region. Where available, use the app’s
    <strong>Ad privacy choices</strong> option to review or change your
    choices. You can also manage advertising identifiers and advertising
    privacy options in your Android device settings. Available settings
    depend on your Android version and region. Limiting personalization
    does not necessarily remove ads or all processing needed to deliver,
    measure, or protect advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Contacting READY COM</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we receive your email address, message, and any
    information or attachments you choose to send. We use them to
    respond, provide support, and handle privacy requests. Email is
    processed through our email service provider, Microsoft Outlook.
    Please send only information needed for your request.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Retention, deletion, and security</h2>
  <p>
    Local app information remains until you remove it, clear the app’s
    storage, or uninstall the app. Saved designs can be deleted within
    the app. Clearing app storage removes local progress and certificate
    information. You must delete separately any files you exported to
    other locations.
  </p>
  <p>
    Support correspondence is retained only for as long as needed to
    handle the request and relevant legal obligations. Advertising
    partners determine retention for information they process, as
    described in their policies. We take reasonable care with
    information under our control, but no device, transmission, or
    storage method can guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights and international processing</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct,
    delete, or obtain a copy of personal information, restrict or object
    to processing, withdraw consent, or complain to a data-protection
    authority. Contact us at the email above for information under
    READY COM’s control. For information controlled by advertising
    providers, use their privacy contacts and controls. Withdrawing
    consent does not affect earlier lawful processing.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where applicable law requires a legal basis, consent is used for
    advertising activities that require it; support requests and service
    security are handled on the applicable service-related or
    legitimate-interest basis. Providers explain their own legal bases
    and safeguards in their policies. Email and advertising services may
    process information outside your country, subject to their stated
    safeguards and applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Children’s privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Parents or guardians who believe a child has provided personal
    information to READY COM should contact us so we can investigate
    and take appropriate steps. Avoid including a child’s full name
    or other identifying details in support messages unless necessary.
    Advertising providers’ policies describe their handling of
    children’s information and applicable privacy protections.
  </p>

  <h2>9. This policy page and future changes</h2>
  <p>
    This page includes no analytics scripts, advertising, or forms.
    The hosting service may process technical request information,
    such as IP addresses and server logs, to deliver and secure the
    page. If the app’s data practices change, we will update this
    policy and its date, and provide additional notice when required.
  </p>

  <footer>
    <strong>READY COM</strong>
    <p>
      Privacy and support:
      <a href="mailto:kolonil97@outlook.com">kolonil97@outlook.com</a>
    </p>
  </footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
